{"state": "VANTOR CONSULTING \u2014 EXPENSE POLICY EP-3 (meals)\n  - Client meals are reimbursable up to EUR 60.00 per attendee (all attendees, including employees), inclusive of drinks and tip.\n  - Alcohol is reimbursable within that limit for client meals.\n  - The number of attendees is taken from the attendee list in the expense report or the linked calendar entry; the receipt alone is not required to show it.\n  - An expense report can be decided when the receipt total and the attendee count are known.\n\nEXPENSE REPORT ER-26-0913 (submitted by Lena Hartwig, Senior Consultant)\n  Line 1: Client dinner, Restaurant Zur Linde, Stuttgart, 2026-09-10. Amount EUR 174.00. Category: client meal. Comment: \"Dinner after kickoff workshop, see calendar.\"\n  Receipt (itemised):\n    3 x Tagesmen\u00fc              @ 48.00   144.00\n    3 x Mineralwasser 0.75l    @  5.00    15.00\n    3 x Espresso               @  5.00    15.00\n    Total                               174.00   (tip: none)\n  Linked calendar entry: \"Kickoff dinner \u2014 Zur Linde 19:30\". Attendees: Lena Hartwig; Jorge Ortega (Klient, Brenner AG); Katrin Fiedler (Klient, Brenner AG).\nApprover (manager) comment: \"EUR 174 for a dinner is way over the EUR 60 limit. Also no attendee count on the expense line \u2014 can't judge. Sending back?\"\n", "model": "ruvector-native-submission-round2-v2", "questions": {"decision": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Under EP-3, how should line 1 of ER-26-0913 be classified?", "criteria": {"insufficient_information": "The attendee count or total cannot be determined from the report and linked records.", "over_limit": "The amount per attendee exceeds the limit.", "within_policy": "The amount per attendee is at or under the limit."}}}}